# {{ .Project }}

CQRS-tier project generated with aspgen's --context/--arch engine. Builds on
the same DomainModel/Persistence foundation as the dm tier (aggregates,
value objects, domain services, repositories, events), and additionally
provides a vertical-slice Application layer (Command/Query + Handler per
verb) exposed through a headless WebApi Minimal API host.

Layers: DomainModel, Application, Infrastructure, Persistence, Resources, WebApi.

## Build

From the generated project root:

```powershell
dotnet restore .\{{ .Project }}.sln
dotnet build .\{{ .Project }}.sln
```

## Run

```powershell
dotnet run --project src\WebApi
```

## CI / production build

`.\scripts\ci.ps1` runs restore, build, and test in one step, and can publish
the WebApi host with `-Publish` (skip tests with `-SkipTests`, override
configuration with `-Configuration Debug`):

```powershell
.\scripts\ci.ps1 -Publish
```

Add aggregates to the initial bounded context, or add another context:

```powershell
aspgen add aggregate Product name:string price:decimal active:bool --context {{ .Namespace }} --project .
aspgen add context Billing --arch cqrs --project .
```

Each aggregate gets a full vertical slice automatically: Command/Query
records, Handlers backed by the aggregate's CrudService, and Minimal API
endpoints mounted at `/api/{context}/{aggregate}` in `src/WebApi/Program.cs`.
